findings.citation_text:
4-602.13 The following nonfood contact surfaces were observed to be soiled:
A) bottom area on back side of salad cooler where grated cover is missing (cheese shreds/general debris);
B) bottom inside oven in dining area (carbon buildup); 
C) drip tray of pizza oven in dining area (carbon/food debris);  and
D) counter under tea and coffee machines (general debris).
Nonfood contact surfaces shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to eliminate buildup of grease, food splash and general debris.

findings.comment:
750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) black freezer (bottom inside - food debris);
B) large prep cooler (bottom inside/general surfaces - food splash);
C) small prep cooler (bottom inside/general surfaces; storage containers w/deli meat - food debris/splash);
D) table top flat grill (waste pan - grease);
E) under food warmers (dust/debris);
F) fryers (general surfaces w/grease and food crumbs);   and
G) prep table across from kitchen 3 part sink (food debris/general buildup; unused equipment with splash).

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.
